WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.416 --> 00:00:41.583


2
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:45.208
<b>As the two armies sounded the call for battle, </b>

3
00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:49.166
<b>Arjuna addressed Lord Krishna, saying, </b>

4
00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:50.666
<b>"O Achyuta!</b>

5
00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:54.458
<b> Drive my chariot between the two armies.</b>

6
00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:58.333
<b>To thoroughly observe all</b>
<b>the warriors assembled on this battlefield </b>

7
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:05.625
<b>and determine whom I must fight is my priority.</b>

8
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:08.958
<b>Until then keep me placed there."</b>

9
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:13.833


10
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:14.833
<b>Here, </b>

11
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:18.083
<b>Arjuna addresses Krishna as "Achyuta," </b>

12
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:18.958
<b>"Achyuta,"</b>

13
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:26.833
<b>meaning the infallible one, the immovable,</b>

14
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.333
<b>Arjuna was a devotee of Lord Krishna, </b>

15
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:33.541
<b>knowing him to be God incarnate. </b>

16
00:01:33.541 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>Such is Krishna's love </b>

17
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:37.875
<b>for his devotees </b>

18
00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:40.375
<b>that, despite being the</b>
<b>master of the entire creation, </b>

19
00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:43.541
<b>he humbly and joyfully</b>

20
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:47.708
<b>accepted the role of Arjuna's charioteer. </b>

21
00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:53.666
<b>He agreed to take Arjuna's chariot</b>
<b>wherever he desired.</b>

22
00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:54.958
<b>And here, Arjuna</b>

23
00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:57.625
<b>wishes to go to the center of the battlefield. </b>

24
00:01:57.625 --> 00:01:59.333
<b>He wants to observe, </b>

25
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.708
<b>He wants to observe,</b>

26
00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:07.125
<b>against whom he must fight this war.</b>

27
00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:11.875


28
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:15.166
<b>The war horns have sounded;  </b>

29
00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:19.083
<b>at any moment, weapons will clash. </b>

30
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:20.416
<b>In such times,</b>

31
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:24.125
<b>warriors are eager to display their prowess. </b>

32
00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:25.666
<b>But </b>

33
00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:28.375
<b>Arjuna, instead of raising his Gandiva</b>

34
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:31.541
<b>bow and readying his arrows, </b>

35
00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:36.041
<b>He pauses thoughtfully. </b>

36
00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:38.875
<b>He wants to reflect </b>

37
00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:41.583
<b>on what he is about to do. </b>

38
00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:45.416
<b>A great war is no small matter, my friends. </b>

39
00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:49.791
<b>To be contemplative even in</b>
<b>such dire circumstances</b>

40
00:02:49.791 --> 00:02:52.791
<b>is a virtuous quality.</b>

41
00:02:52.791 --> 00:02:55.375
<b>Now you tell me, </b>

42
00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:01.541
<b>do you rush to act at the first sign of trouble? </b>

43
00:03:01.541 --> 00:03:05.958
<b>Do you immediately draw your</b>
<b>weapons and charge in? </b>

44
00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:09.333
<b>Or do you pause </b>

45
00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:17.250
<b>to consider whether your initial impulse is</b>
<b>the right course of action? Or not?</b>

46
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.958
<b>Does it feel </b>

47
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:22.208
<b>like the hands of the clock are racing, </b>

48
00:03:22.208 --> 00:03:24.458
<b>that even 24 hours are not enough, </b>

49
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:28.250
<b>that you must be constantly doing something? </b>

50
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.208
<b>contemplation or meditation is a waste of time? </b>

51
00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:35.208
<b>Is this how you feel?</b>

52
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:36.500
<b>If Yes, </b>

53
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.125
<b>Then this merely is restlessness.</b>

54
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:46.333
<b>If Arjuna can find a few moments</b>
<b>for reflection on the battlefield,</b>

55
00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:51.500
<b>then what great battles are you</b>
<b>fighting in your daily life?</b>

56
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:59.333
<b>Surely, you too can spare a few moments</b>
<b>for contemplation or meditation before acting. </b>

57
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.458
<b>It will be for your own benefit.</b>

58
00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:06.125


59
00:04:06.125 --> 00:04:09.666
<b>Surely you've experienced this: </b>

60
00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.916
<b>someone says something, </b>

61
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:14.541
<b>you fire back a retort, </b>

62
00:04:14.541 --> 00:04:16.083
<b>they respond,</b>

63
00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:23.333
<b>they respond, and so on, until</b>
<b>a molehill becomes a mountain</b>

64
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:25.250
<b>A dispute arises. </b>

65
00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.458
<b>Resentment grows between two people. </b>

66
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:30.583
<b>If not to you,</b>

67
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:35.250
<b>you've certainly seen this happen somewhere. </b>

68
00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.416
<b>Well,</b>

69
00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:41.166
<b>the biggest root of conflict is knee-jerk reactions. </b>

70
00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:45.125
<b>It's as if there's a race to see who will win. </b>

71
00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:47.541
<b>The sad thing is, </b>

72
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:54.291
<b>when thoughtless discord arises in relationships, </b>

73
00:04:54.291 --> 00:04:56.250
<b>both the parties lose.</b>

74
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.291
<b>Just as Arjuna </b>

75
00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:03.083
<b>pauses to reflect before proceeding into the battle, </b>

76
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:12.375
<b>if you also take a moment, to think, before reacting,</b>
<b>half of these disputes will end before they begin.</b>

77
00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:17.125
<b>Harmony will prevail in your social relationships.</b>

78
00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:21.750


79
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.791
<b>An email arrives. </b>

80
00:05:23.791 --> 00:05:24.875
<b>"Hey! </b>

81
00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:27.166
<b>How could they say that to me, </b>

82
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:29.375
<b>and that too in front of everyone?" </b>

83
00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:31.541
<b>And you immediately </b>

84
00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:34.416
<b>compose a long, detailed reply. </b>

85
00:05:34.416 --> 00:05:35.875
<b>To everyone. </b>

86
00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:40.000
<b>Then you remember you made a huge mistake, </b>

87
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.125
<b>or notice a line you hadn't read before. </b>

88
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:52.541
<b>And now you're trying to figure out</b>
<b>how to stop that message from reaching people.</b>

89
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>Be honest, </b>

90
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:57.125
<b>this has happened to you too, right? </b>

91
00:05:57.125 --> 00:06:00.583
<b>Or something similar.</b>

92
00:06:00.583 --> 00:06:02.708
<b>A big project comes in, </b>

93
00:06:02.708 --> 00:06:04.541
<b>time is short, </b>

94
00:06:04.541 --> 00:06:06.375
<b>you become flustered. </b>

95
00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:08.583
<b>"How will this get done? It's impossible!" </b>

96
00:06:08.583 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>Take a moment to think </b>

97
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:19.208
<b>is there someone who navigates</b>
<b>these situations with ease? </b>

98
00:06:19.208 --> 00:06:20.875
<b>What's the difference </b>

99
00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:25.625
<b>between their approach and yours?</b>

100
00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:30.416
<b>The answer is always the same. </b>

101
00:06:30.416 --> 00:06:35.416
<b>That person works with a sense of calm. </b>

102
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:37.458
<b>In professional life, </b>

103
00:06:37.458 --> 00:06:43.000
<b>calm and competent are synonymous.   </b>

104
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.291
<b>The calm one </b>

105
00:06:45.291 --> 00:06:48.125
<b>is the wise one</b>

